{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"ALL 7 ACs MET — evidence, ready to close.\n\nLanded as Gerrit change 1064 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, MERGED). The superseded compaction\nrevision 1060 is ABANDONED in Gerrit so it cannot be submitted.\n\nAC-by-AC:\n 1. Both blocked tickets reach a verdict: the cap is 100,000 chars, covering 9fd4 (34,282) and\n    2932/db1c (41,595) with ~2.4x headroom. Test parameterized on those two measured sizes.\n 2. Context byte-identical: a test asserts every per-criterion call carries the assembled context\n    VERBATIM, so reintroducing elision fails. Mutation-verified (truncating the context in\n    _recover turns it red).\n 3. criteria <= context invariant: pinned by test; mutation-verified (setting the cap back to\n    24,000 turns it red).\n 4. Over-cap fails fast with ZERO billable recovery calls, asserted by call count.\n 5. Step-budget failure no longer blames a missing extra — PROVEN LIVE: the gate now says \"The\n    completion verifier ran and then failed, so this is not a missing install or credential — act\n    on its own reported remedy ... Raise REBAR_LLM_MAX_STEPS\". Genuine unavailability still gets\n    the install-the-extra guidance (negative control retained).\n 6. docs/llm-framework.md states the 100,000 cap, that nothing is elided, and why compaction was\n    withdrawn.\n 7. Landed with both votes; 1060 abandoned.\n\nWHY COMPACTION WAS WITHDRAWN (the important part of this ticket's history). An earlier revision\ncompacted an over-cap context by dropping comment history oldest-first. Adversarial review proved\nit a SIGNED-FALSE-PASS vector: on an epic the gate assembles one block PER TICKET\n(assemble_context(graph=True)), each with its own \"#### Comments\" heading, so the elision silently\ndeleted WHOLE CHILD TICKETS — including their unmet acceptance criteria — while reporting only\nthat comments were removed. Reproduced directly. Elision is unsafe in BOTH directions: dropping\nevidence a criterion IS met causes a false FAIL; dropping evidence it is NOT causes a false PASS.\nA refusal is a visible false-block; a bad elision is an invisible signed false PASS, and this gate\nSIGNS its verdict.\n\nNOT IN SCOPE, deliberately: this does not make every large ticket verifiable. The remaining\nfailure modes (turn exhaustion on genuine breadth; output-token truncation into a degraded\nrecovery whose evidence stage is pinned at 4,096 by a min() no operator knob can lift) are\n[rebar:a89d-4dd2-f421-417a], filed with all measurements."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785461753954582001,"uuid":"7e23248f-12e2-4675-80b5-ee8e3228818d"}